ir3: use nearest-even for floating-point conversions without a declared mode.

The zero-initialized cov round field means ROUND_ZERO, so dynamic integer
conversions can disagree with NIR's constant folding. Preserve explicit RTNE
and RTZ controls, including the dedicated f2f16 operations. Default to the same
nearest-even behavior as NIR when float controls leave the mode undefined.
Adapted to the pinned Mesa revision; no Gallium/AIR frontend dependency.

--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_compiler_nir.c
@@ -408,6 +408,12 @@
          set_cat1_round(cov.rpts, nrpt, ROUND_EVEN);
       else if (rounding_mode == nir_rounding_mode_rtz)
          set_cat1_round(cov.rpts, nrpt, ROUND_ZERO);
+      else
+         /* The zero-initialized field is ROUND_ZERO. Match NIR's default
+          * nearest-even conversions when no float-control mode is declared.
+          * Explicit f2f16 operations and float controls are handled above.
+          */
+         set_cat1_round(cov.rpts, nrpt, ROUND_EVEN);
    }
 
    return cov;
